=== backtest↔live parity — six defects + checklist (PROTOCOL ONLY) ===
cite: arXiv:2610.21846 — Where Backtests and Live Trading Part Ways: Six Defects from One Intraday System
NO PnL claim; NO broker API; NO advertised Sharpe — protocol / asserts only
  defect[CAUGHT] feed_ne_SIP_open_vol: live/bt open-vol ratio=0.080
  defect[CAUGHT] div_adjusted_vs_unadjusted: adj-raw=0.0100
  defect[CAUGHT] sizing_past_live_limit: target=2.2 > live_max=1.5
  defect[CAUGHT] UTC_ne_NY: UTC-14 labeled as NY-14 (true NY≈10) — clock defect
  defect[CAUGHT] live_downloads_missing_in_replay: missing_in_replay=['corp_actions.csv', 'halts.csv']
  defect[CAUGHT] config_on_ne_wired: kill flag True but submit path never reads it
synthetic_parity_asserts: caught=6/6 OK
10-point parity checklist:
  1. Same raw feed class in BT and live (SIP vs thin/default) — compare open volume share
  2. Same price adjustment policy (div-adjusted research ≠ unadjusted live tickets)
  3. Sizing clipped to live account / broker limits before submit
  4. Explicit timezone: store UTC, convert to session TZ once; never relabel
  5. Replay includes every live download artifact (halts, corp actions, calendars)
  6. Config flags that gate risk must be wired into the submit path (integration test)
  7. Fill model documented: next-open / mid / touch — frozen for the paper window
  8. Cost model shared object between research and paper (no silent upgrade)
  9. VERSION string frozen; config hash logged each session
  10. Daily recon: strategy ledger vs independent fill replay; break → pause
REJECT: using this paper as a profitability claim; QuantAgent/HFT latency recipes; broker order routers
disclaimer: synthetic paper loop — learning only; no broker connectivity
